{"author":"schacon@gmail.com","body":"Allow defining automations that trigger on ticket state changes. Rules stored in project metadata so they sync with the repo.\n\nExample: when a ticket moves to \"review\", auto-assign a reviewer. When moved to \"closed\", clear the code field.\n\nPossible design:\n- ti workflow add --on \"state:review\" --set \"assigned=lead@example.com\"\n- ti workflow add --on \"state:closed\" --clear code\n- ti workflow list\n- ti workflow remove <id>\n\nRules would be evaluated by the ti state/close commands when they change state. Each rule is: trigger (state change pattern) + action (set/clear/add-tag/etc)."}